Track 2: Siete Veces Deshecho (Seven Times Unraveled)
- Story & Context: Elara, a novice weaver, confessed to the Abbess that she had been intentionally misaligning the modular pulses to hide her secret memories of a seaside life she never lived. She felt the heavy weight of the wool tapestry she carried, its texture rough and smelling of sea salt, as she watched the Abbess burn her favorite M1 patch bank in a brass basin. "I am the fraying edge of a song forgotten," she sang, her voice devoid of vibrato, while the rhythm sputtered and collapsed.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of hands with ink-stained fingertips unraveling a complex, glowing-fiber tapestry, the loose threads transforming into wisps of smoke against a dark, velvet background.

Track 3: The Weaver’s Last Calibration
- Story & Context: Long after the monastery was abandoned to the shifting mountain sands, the final automated patch is still playing in the central hall, recording the wind whistling through the rotted wooden rafters. A local traveler finds the hall filled with sentient, shifting dust clouds that pulse in perfect 115 BPM time to the ancient M1 chords. The traveler leaves a copper coin on the altar, listening as the machine seems to mimic the chime of the falling metal, finally closing the loop. "History is a knot I refused to untie," the machine-voice synthesized into the rafters.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A panoramic view of an abandoned stone monastery hall, sunlight slicing through dust-filled air, with abstract, glowing geometric lattices floating in the center of the room.

